# The cache policy for stored coding procedures (issue #1165, E130).
#
# A stored procedure is a cache entry, never knowledge — every row must name
# where a rediscovery would start from, and a test may delete the whole cache
# file and reproduce every row through research_coding_skill_gap.
program_cache_policy
  version "1"
  purpose "A stored coding procedure is a cache entry, not knowledge. Every row names the query and the documented source a rediscovery starts from, so deleting the cache and re-running research reproduces each row with the same content_id."
  cache_file "data/cache/coding-procedure-cache.lino"
  cache_file_header "The rediscoverable coding-procedure cache (issue #1165, E130).\n\nRuntime cache, not knowledge. The policy that governs every row lives in\ndata/seed/program-cache-policy.lino. A row appears here only after\nresearch_coding_skill_gap verified a procedure against its expected\noutput, and the committed rows may be deleted by a test that then\nreproduces them through the same research path."
  content_hash "fnv1a64 of the entry program bytes"
  grammar_seed "data/seed/program-cst-grammars.lino"
  entry_requires
    rediscovery_query "required"
    rediscovery_source "required"
    entry "required"
    verified_output "required"
    content_id "recomputed on store"
  knows_language_rule "a grammar exists in the grammar seed and discovery found a procedure, either as a cache row or as the bootstrap record of a discovery that already ran"
  bootstrap
    active "true"
    owner "rust/src/knowledge.rs ORACLE_SNAPSHOTS"
    purpose "The embedded snapshots are the record of discovery that ran before the cache file existed, so offline lookups keep answering while the first live refresh materializes rows."
    retirement "Delete the bootstrap record in this seed to stop serving the snapshots with no Rust change, then delete ORACLE_SNAPSHOTS once every language row it covered is reproduced by a rediscovery run."
  miss_route
    purpose "What a write_program cache miss needs before research_coding_skill_gap can run on it. Research verifies a candidate against an expected output under a reviewer's approval; a solve call carries the task's expected output from the program seed but no reviewer approval, so the solver records the miss with every input it lacks instead of answering as if research had run."
    research_requires "expected_output"
    research_requires "reviewer_approval"
    solve_carries "expected_output"
  documentation_route
    active "true"
    captures "data/seed/coding-documentation-captures.lino"
    purpose "A write_program cache miss whose language and task have documentation captures rediscovers its program from them at answer time. In each captured page the first block, in the requested language or untagged, that decomposes into an output call printing a literal is recomposed with the task's expected output bound into that literal, and the shortest such program is kept. It is answered only when decomposing it again finds the same output call printing the expected output, and when it declares every name the language's run contract invokes (the save_as stem a run or check command names bare). The row it yields cites the page as its rediscovery_source and its rediscovery_query, and is stored when the solve has a writable runtime cache (FORMAL_AI_PROCEDURE_CACHE), so the next request reuses it as a hit. The committed cache file is never written by a solve."
    verification "decomposition"
    verification "run_contract"
